  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "route_continuity",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "All 121 selected nodes, 161 requires edges, categories, gate kinds and statuses are unchanged from v0.38. No selected node is orphaned, no reference is missing and the logical graph is acyclic. Both root reachability counts and the exact I/II/V versus I/II/III/V distinction are independently verified."
    },
    {
      "id": "topDesWin",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "The pinned DesWin.lean signature still has hEx and nine Closed predicates plus h1,h2,hV. Both root gates preserve those ten contracts and constants (2,3,2,0), one common class and one Fm,CH only after the common Closed threshold. There is no independent gap shortcut or construction from unrelated families."
    },
    {
      "id": "complete_vs_open",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "There are exactly 33 unchanged open compound leaves: 22 C, 9 B and 2 D. The eight new nested closures do not close a whole leaf. Implication certificates, genuine arithmetic producers and nonsufficient work-refinement links remain distinct. Fullness still excludes GL4 and final slope assembly."
    },
    {
      "id": "row_integrability",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "RPI14 supplies all actual row products and translates on MY0, fd0 and ofReal(nP^-1)nu0. RPI15 discharges only the added RowPairInt premise; original readings, Pins/Holds, five real-group predicates, stored nonzero chain and group tie remain. The graph does not infer universal quotient-height CuspRapidDecay or the stronger second DivRows3."
    },
    {
      "id": "actual_readings",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "RDR12, RDR20 and RDR21 are recorded as the complete original given-data constructors, with one Side0 before every later reader and simultaneous exact map ties. Full ReadL remains guarded by o.eta(j,v)=q.eta(j,v) on every 1<=j<=m and place. Actual ChT/LfT/Reps/Fits/Moved, primitive tests and common realization remain C inputs. The completed constructor is not promoted to a new family member or threshold."
    },
    {
      "id": "entire_S4",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "LIM proves the full original universal S4 on T.ProL, with one cover and ultrafilter and uniform whole-map local convergence; it is not restricted to the selected h=0 instance. The current count cut removes S4 from residuals and retains actual normalized patched rings/maps/modules and S5 support."
    },
    {
      "id": "full_proell_descent",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "PQL supplies full original TWQuot and CoreBC-to-Raw, including full determinant laws, closed ideals, same B,J,K,f, supplied TWAut and the needed one-way NonSS implication. This agrees with the pinned distinct Core/CoreBC/Raw definitions. Core-to-CoreBC coefficient normalization, the added Unit parameter and normalized Core/S5 are still explicit; descent of supplied finite-level modules is not claimed to construct a patched module."
    },
    {
      "id": "count_same_ideal",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "Both original rank-four Links retain fixed iota, ell=3, one coefficient threshold before every later DVR/B/Lambda, and one J for all seven duties. The selected h=0,a=n=4,g=0 Choice/B1/B2 remain one coupled witness, with one B1 constant before m and the original eventual-N guards. Full CohP, LocCFT, N4, residual-cyclotomic and local guards remain; no arbitrary-Kap result or Sel1=0 is inferred."
    },
    {
      "id": "count_field_and_target",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "Count I keeps Kstar(pK chi), principal Q(sqrt(-7)); Count V keeps its distinct Gaussian/quartic field. The principal Count-V e=1, ell in {3,7} restriction is explicit and the stronger universal host implementation is not labelled necessary. Case III is absent only for the principal/two-primary route and remains on unrestricted Dirichlet GRH."
    },
    {
      "id": "open_route_coverage",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "Independently intersecting root reachability with the unchanged open-leaf set gives 26 RH leaves, all shared with Dirichlet GRH, and 33 GRH leaves. Shared categories are C18/B6/D2; the seven additional GRH leaves are exactly the Case-III seed/chain/assembly tasks. The derived route_coverage.json is hash-bound and accurately labels these as dependency counts rather than difficulty weights or completion percentages."
    },
    {
      "id": "historical_current_boundary",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "All predecessor interface cuts and 245 historical target records are retained. The three new v0.39 interface cuts and additive record updates govern current scope; preserved historical S4/RowPairInt descriptions are not current residuals. Original IDs, including originally absent IDs represented by the established stable record IDs, indices, hashes and all old scopes are preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "narrative_register",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "All 33 contracts were read individually and checked byte-for-byte between graph and leaf register, verbatim in the standalone TXT and exactly after reversing typesetting escapes in main.tex. The opening summaries, 77 new/1998 cumulative claim counts, classifications, narrower nested closures and next priorities agree with the four current component closures."
    },
    {
      "id": "source_identity",
      "status": "PASS",
      "finding": "All 14 current graph inputs and all embedded component evidence are hash-bound. All 596 distinct graph source ranges in 207 files were checked against the pinned Git blobs; source locations and hashes are consistent. All four independent current component reviews pass on the exact released bytes and jointly cover 77 claims."
    }
  ],
